      <Docs>
        <param name="key">the extension key</param>
        <param name="value">the extension value</param>
        <summary>Sets the extension for the given key.</summary>
        <returns>This builder.</returns>
        <remarks>
          <para>Sets the extension for the given key. A null or empty value requests removal. On Android 5 and 6, removal matches the key with its original case; on Android 7 through 17, it is case-insensitive. A non-empty value is checked for valid syntax. The key UNICODE_LOCALE_EXTENSION ('u') is used for the Unicode locale extension. On Android 7 through 17, setting this key replaces existing Unicode locale keywords and attributes; a null or empty value clears them. On Android 5 and 6, a null or empty value does not clear those keywords or attributes. A non-empty value clears other extensions and the Unicode attributes, sets the parsed keywords, and retains existing keywords not in the new value. The key PRIVATE_USE_EXTENSION ('x') is used for the private use code. To be well-formed, the value for this key needs only to have subtags of one to eight alphanumeric characters, not two to eight as in the general case.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/java/util/Locale.Builder.html#setExtension(char,java.lang.String)" title="Reference documentation">Java reference for <code>java.util.Locale.Builder.setExtension</code>.</a></format></para>
          <para>Portions of this page are modifications based on work created and shared by the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/site-policies" title="Android Open Source Project">Android Open Source Project</a></format> and used according to terms described in the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5/" title="Creative Commons 2.5 Attribution License">Creative Commons 2.5 Attribution License.</a></format></para>
        </remarks>
      </Docs>
