      <Docs>
        <param name="languageTag">the language tag</param>
        <summary>Resets the Builder to match the provided IETF BCP 47 language tag.</summary>
        <returns>This builder.</returns>
        <remarks>
          <para>Resets the Builder to match the provided IETF BCP 47 language tag. For a well-formed tag, it discards the existing state. On Android 5 and 6, a null or empty tag resets the builder. On Android 7 through 17, null throws <see cref="T:Java.Lang.NullPointerException" /> and an empty tag throws <see cref="T:Java.Util.IllformedLocaleException" />. Legacy tags (see Locale.forLanguageTag(java.lang.String)) are converted to their canonical form before being processed. Otherwise, the language tag must be well-formed (see Locale) or an exception is thrown (unlike Locale.forLanguageTag, which just discards ill-formed and following portions of the tag).</para>
