      <Docs>
        <param name="locale">the locale</param>
        <summary>Resets the Builder to match the provided locale.</summary>
        <returns>This builder.</returns>
        <remarks>
          <para>Resets the Builder to match the provided locale. On success, existing state is discarded. The locale's language, region and variant are validated, and an ill-formed value causes IllformedLocaleException to be thrown. On Android 7 through 17, the script is also validated and the following three cases are accepted for compatibility reasons: Locale("ja", "JP", "JP") is treated as "ja-JP-u-ca-japanese"; Locale("th", "TH", "TH") is treated as "th-TH-u-nu-thai"; Locale("no", "NO", "NY") is treated as "nn-NO". Android 5 and 6 reject these three cases because their variants are ill-formed.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/java/util/Locale.Builder.html#setLocale(java.util.Locale)" title="Reference documentation">Java reference for <code>java.util.Locale.Builder.setLocale</code>.</a></format></para>
