        <param name="key">the Unicode locale key</param>
        <param name="type">the Unicode locale type</param>
        <summary>Sets the Unicode locale keyword type for the given key.</summary>
        <returns>This builder.</returns>
        <remarks>
          <para>Sets the Unicode locale keyword type for the given key. The key must be non-null. If the type is null, the method attempts to remove the keyword. On Android 5 and 6, removal uses the key with its original case and does not check whether the key is well-formed. On Android 7 through 17, the key must be well-formed and is matched without regard to case. If the type is not null, the key and type are checked for valid syntax. Android 5 and 6 reject an empty type, while Android 7 through 17 allow it. Stored keys and types are converted to lower case. On Android 7 through 17, setting the 'u' extension via setExtension(char, java.lang.String) replaces all Unicode locale keywords with those defined in the extension. On Android 5 and 6, existing keywords that are not in the new extension are retained.</para>
          <para><format type="text/html"><a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/21/docs/api/java.base/java/util/Locale.Builder.html#setUnicodeLocaleKeyword(java.lang.String,java.lang.String)" title="Reference documentation">Java reference for <code>java.util.Locale.Builder.setUnicodeLocaleKeyword</code>.</a></format></para>
          <para>Portions of this page are modifications based on work created and shared by the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/site-policies" title="Android Open Source Project">Android Open Source Project</a></format> and used according to terms described in the <format type="text/html"><a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.5/" title="Creative Commons 2.5 Attribution License">Creative Commons 2.5 Attribution License.</a></format></para>
